---
description: LoRa AMP, star v1, SQLite, no MQTT on core ingest. Frozen AMP spec is not rewritten here.
globs:
  - gateway/**
  - backend/**
  - database/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Comms / gateway / database

- Radio payload is untrusted. Validate frame, CRC, version, schema, node ID; then de-dup and sequence analysis.
- AMP Protocol Version 1 remains on the wire (ADR-006). `uint16` `wire_id`; registry `display_id` (e.g. NODE-03). ADR-009.
- Physical: SX1278 433 MHz, star v1. Do not retune to 868/915. Do not casually rewrite AMP_PROTOCOL_SPEC.md.
- `measurement_time` and `received_at` stay separate. TIME_SYNC without GNSS (ADR-010). Missing ≠ zero.
- SQLite v1 behind a repository (ADR-014). `sampling_decisions` mandatory. Dashboard/AI must not open the DB file.
- MQTT is not on the core path (ADR-015): radio → validate → ingest → SQLite → intelligence → API/WebSocket.

This rule does not override AMP or DOC-004 until those documents are formally revised.
